  "lo'i mi .e la djan" is not grammatical because "lo'i"  (being a LE) can
only take a brivla (with perhaps an inner qualifier).  If followed by a
KOhA, it will assume it's a "pe"-type qualifier (e.g. like "lo me gerku").
 lu'i on the otgher hand, specifically takes sumti and makes them into
other sumti types.
          --gejyspa


